<title>ITALY: CYCLING-RESULTS AND STANDINGS OF TIRRENO-ADRIATICO.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-RESULTS AND STANDINGS OF TIRRENO-ADRIATICO.</headline>
<dateline>NARNI, Italy 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of the</p>
<p>third 213-km stage of the Tirreno-Adriatico cycle race on</p>
<p>Saturday (Italians unless stated):</p>
<p>1. Michele Bartoli four hours 48 minutes 52 seconds</p>
<p>2. Francesco Casagrande</p>
<p>3. Gabriele Colombo</p>
<p>4. Roberto Petito</p>
<p>5. Gianluca Pianegonda</p>
<p>6. Maurizio Fondriest</p>
<p>7. Sergio Previtali</p>
<p>8. Andrea Ferrigato all same time</p>
<p>9. Beat Zberg (Switzerland) four seconds</p>
<p>10.Stefano Della Santa six seconds</p>
<p>Overall standings:</p>
<p>1. Petito 13 hours 14 minutes 31 seconds</p>
<p>2. Pianegonda same time</p>
<p>3. Zberg 12 seconds</p>
<p>4. Massimiliano Gentili 23 seconds</p>
<p>5. Davide Casarotto 24 seconds</p>
<p>6. Francesco Frattini 26 seconds</p>
<p>7. Vassily Davidenko (Russia) 35 seconds</p>
<p>8. Luc Leblanc (France) 41 seconds</p>
<p>9. Massimo Donati 55 seconds</p>
<p>10.Bartoli two minutes 47 seconds</p>
</text>
